domain ADR0037:
  description "ADR-0037 revision 1: historical fragment proposal. Status Rejected after replacement by ADR-0038."

problem P1:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0006 publishes narrator prose only as a validated terminal
    snapshot and keeps provider progress private. The product owner now directs
    provisional Streaming display, visible retry, and immutable Fragment-level
    Commit. The public prose decisions conflict and need an explicit successor.

evidence OWNER_DIRECTION:
  |
    On 2026-09-29 the owner described a Battle with one logical Narration,
    immutable Fragments accumulating within it, and a Fragment committed only
    after its Streaming is received successfully to completion. The owner also
    directed that a failed attempt retains its partial display, displays a
    retrying message when retry is scheduled, and replaces that display when
    the first content chunk of the new attempt arrives. The owner said the
    attempt need not reproduce the same Streaming and Narration success or
    failure does not alter Battle canonical history. The subsequent request
    to fix these decisions in design and policy authorizes drafting this ADR,
    not acceptance of its exact revision.

evidence PRIOR_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0006 chose terminal-snapshot-only prose over public partial
    prose with visible reset. It also specifies receipt identity, ordered
    finite battle delivery, durable cursor and outbox, at-least-once delivery,
    fixed canonical input, worker fencing, and Battle advance independence.
    Accepted ADR-0016 and ADR-0017 define existing Beat and Turn clocks.

premise SCOPE:
  |
    This proposal changes the representation and public presentation of
    Narration prose and its generation attempts. It does not change Battle
    canonical facts, Turn or Beat semantics, queue provider, authorization,
    worker fencing, release, production data, or acceptance of this ADR.
    Application to existing and in-progress battles and clients remains an
    owner decision before migration or implementation is specified.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Keep ADR-0006 terminal-only prose, which preserves simple historical
    replay but fails the new Streaming direction; stream mutable cumulative
    prose, which allows fast display but lacks immutable Fragment Commit; or
    show attempt-scoped provisional chunks and append a completed immutable
    Fragment per slot, which meets the owner direction with additional client
    attempt-state and recovery rules.

decision D1 based_on P1, OWNER_DIRECTION, PRIOR_AUTHORITY, OPTIONS:
  |
    Propose the third option. One logical Narration belongs to each Battle and
    accumulates zero or more ordered committed Fragments. The complete text,
    order, and source references of each committed Fragment are immutable.
    Attempt chunks are provisional and never become a Fragment merely because
    they were displayed. A Fragment is committed only after successful source
    completion and durable atomic storage. One slot can have at most one
    committed Fragment even when attempts or deliveries repeat.

decision D2 based_on D1, OWNER_DIRECTION:
  |
    Propose that a failed attempt leaves its provisional display visible.
    A scheduled retry adds a retrying indication. Starting the new attempt
    does not clear the prior display; its first content chunk clears the
    previous provisional display and indication for that slot before showing
    new chunks. If retries end without Commit, retain provisional text and
    show terminal failure. Attempt replay and chunk identity across attempts
    are not required. A committed Fragment replaces provisional display with
    its complete authoritative text.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, PRIOR_AUTHORITY, SCOPE:
  |
    Propose superseding only ADR-0006's terminal-only/public-prose-private
    progress and terminal-block replacement choices. Retain its canonical
    Battle advance independence, immutable input, public receipt identity and battle-local
    ordering, physically finite authenticated reconnectable stream, durable
    cursor and outbox, at-least-once delivery, queue wake-up, and fencing
    decisions. Distinguish transport failure from generation failure; reconnect
    reads committed Fragments. Retain ADR-0016/0017 Turn and Beat meaning.
    Beat-to-Fragment cardinality, provisional recovery after full page reload,
    and adoption scope remain undecided.

evidence OWNER_REPLACEMENT:
  |
    On 2026-09-29 the owner accepted the newer Fragment/observation/memory
    model in discussion and requested a new ADR to overwrite this older
    Proposed candidate. They then confirmed recording the three-clock result
    reveal rule in the new ADR candidate. This is withdrawal of the older
    proposal, not acceptance of ADR-0038's exact text.

decision WITHDRAWAL based_on OWNER_REPLACEMENT, D1, D2, D3:
  |
    Mark ADR-0037 Rejected as a never-Accepted historical proposal replaced
    by Proposed ADR-0038. It does not supersede Accepted ADR-0006/0016 and
    no implementation authority flows from its earlier proposed decisions.
